-- Ordered quest guidance; source 967020b2b8ca645afcaf90d9bbe5a1b64673947d; generated 2026-10-20.
QuestGuidance.Register("en",70,{
[2209]="700001C4\n1\tTalk to Aragorn in Rivendell\tAragorn waits in one of the guest rooms of Elrond's House. Elrond warned you of a growing evil within Angmar and asked you to speak with Aragorn.\n",
[2210]="7002FA6A\n1\tTalk to Adnoth outside Langhold, in the Wold\tYou have travelled with some of Mansig's riders to Langhold, in the Wold, in search of war-steeds for your companions.\n",
[2211]="700465C7\n1\tTravel to Aragorn's Pavilion east of the city, after the battle of Pelennor Fields\tAragorn's pavilion is east of Minas Tirith on the Pelennor Fields, after the battle is concluded. A horse at the Threshold of the City during the Battle of Pelennor Fields will bring you After the Battle.\n2\tTalk to Prince Imrahil at Aragorn's Pavilion\tPrince Imrahil is at Aragorn's Pavilion, east of Minas Tirith, after the Battle of Pelennor Fields.\n3\tFind Elfhelm south-west of Aragorn's Pavilion, on the Pelennor Fields\tElfhelm and Daervunn are south-west of Aragorn's Pavilion on the Pelennor Fields.\n4\tTalk to Elfhelm south-west of Aragorn's Pavilion\030Talk to Daervunn south-west of Aragorn's Pavilion\tElfhelm and Daervunn are south-west of Aragorn's Pavilion on the Pelennor Fields.\n5\tFind Legolas and Gimli at the city gates of Minas Tirith, west of Aragorn's Pavilion\tLegolas and Gimli are outside the city gate of Minas Tirith, after the battle.\n6\tTalk to Legolas at the city gates, west of Aragorn's Pavilion\tLegolas and Gimli are outside the city gate of Minas Tirith, after the battle.\n7\tTalk to Gimli at the city gates, west of Aragorn's Pavilion\tLegolas and Gimli are outside the city gate of Minas Tirith, after the battle.\n8\tTalk to Aragorn at his pavilion on the Pelennor Fields\tAragorn's Pavilion is east of Minas Tirith on the Pelennor Fields, after the battle is concluded.\n",
[2212]="7000019A\n1\tFind the Rangers of Gath Forthnír\tGath Forthnír lies somewhere far to the north of Gabilshathûr. Braigiar has sent you to find and lend aid to the survivors of Golodir's company at the encampment of Gath Forthnír.\n2\tTalk to Lorniel\tLorniel is inside the building at Gath Forthnír. Areneth told you to speak with Lorniel, daughter of Golodir.\n",
[2213]="70018ECB\n1\tTalk to Milwen\tMilwen is by the archway west of the hill of Cerin Amroth, located in the centre of Lothlórien, far to the north-east of Talan Haldir and east of Echad Andestel. You have been told to speak with Milwen on the hill of Cerin Amroth, within the woods of Lórien.\n",
[2214]="7002F976\n1\tTalk to Nona atop the ladder leading down from the flet near the House of Celeborn\tNona is by the ladder down from the flets on which stand the House of Celeborn. Nona is waiting for you to show her around Caras Galadhon.\n2\tTalk to Húrien at Celúrlin, the White Fountain of Caras Galadhon\030Talk to Luidhros on the Telain Galadhrim\030Talk to Anglamel on the Telain Melthin\tNow that Galadriel has given permission for Nona to explore Caras Galadhon, you should bring her to see several of its notable locations: Celúrlin, the White Fountain of Caras Galadhon, and several of the flets where much of the work of the Elves is done: the Telain Galadhrim and Telain Melthin.\n3\tTalk to Galadriel in her garden\tHaving shown Nona around Caras Galadhon, you should now speak with Galadriel in her garden as she requested.\n",
[2215]="7000019B\n1\tTalk to Raghnall\tMeet with Raghnall south of Bail Cátharnakh, west of Gath Forthnír. Lorniel told you that she had heard from a Hillman named Raghnall who was seeking to leave the service of Angmar and might have information that will allow her to gain access to Carn Dûm.\n2\tBring the scroll to Lorniel\tLorniel can be found within Gath Forthnír, east of Bail Cátharnakh. You met with Raghnall and he gave you a scroll that explains how to forge a key for the Gates of Carn Dûm.\n",
[2216]="700465E2\n1\tTalk to Aragorn at his pavilion and help him determine his course\tAragorn is at his pavilion, east of Minas Tirith, after the Battle of Pelennor Fields.\n2\tTalk to Aragorn at his pavilion on the Pelennor Fields\tAragorn is at his pavilion east of Minas Tirith, after the Battle of Pelennor Fields.\n",
[2217]="7002FA12\n1\tPeer into the Mirror of Galadriel and experience 'Session: The Point of Decision' or read the shortened account instead\tThe Mirror of Galadriel is within her garden, in Caras Galadhon. Galadriel has asked you to peer into her mirror and see what awaits the Fellowship on their journey south.\n2\tTalk to Galadriel in her garden\tGaladriel is in her garden in Caras Galadhon. You have peered into her mirror, and should now speak to Galadriel about what you have seen.\n",
[2218]="7000018D\n1\tTalk to Laerdan\tLaerdan is in Gath Forthnír. Lorniel suggested you seek out an Elf named Laerdan in hopes of learning what Raghnall's scroll would reveal.\n2\tBring the scroll to Elrond Halfelven\tElrond Halfelven is at Rivendell in the Trollshaws. Laerdan, also unable to translate the scroll, sent you to Rivendell to speak with Elrond Halfelven.\n",
[2219]="7004663D\n1\tRead aloud Aragorn's call for soldiers (0 Soldiers Pledged to Aragorn)\030Find the herald north-west of Aragorn's Pavilion (0 Soldiers Pledged to Aragorn)\tThere is a herald on the Pelennor Fields north-west of Aragorn's Pavilion. Aragorn sent you to read his call for more soldiers to heralds who can reach the ears of the men that have now arrived at the city.\n2\tFind the herald outside the city gate of Minas Tirith (462 Soldiers Pledged to Aragorn)\tThere is a herald outside the city gate of Minas Tirith. Aragorn sent you to read his call for more soldiers to heralds who can reach the ears of the men that have now arrived at the city.\n3\tRead aloud Aragorn's call for soldiers (1203 Soldiers Pledged to Aragorn)\030Find the herald outside the city gate of Minas Tirith (1003 Soldiers Pledged to Aragorn)\tThere is a herald outside the city gate of Minas Tirith. Aragorn sent you to read his call for more soldiers to heralds who can reach the ears of the men that have now arrived at the city.\n4\tFind the herald inside the city gate of Minas Tirith (1450 Soldiers Pledged to Aragorn)\tThere is a herald inside the city gate of Minas Tirith. Aragorn sent you to read his call for more soldiers to heralds who can reach the ears of the men that have now arrived at the city.\n5\tRead aloud Aragorn's call for soldiers (1802 Soldiers Pledged to Aragorn)\030Find the herald inside the city gate of Minas Tirith (1698 Soldiers Pledged to Aragorn)\tThere is a herald inside the city gate of Minas Tirith. Aragorn sent you to read his call for more soldiers to heralds who can reach the ears of the men that have now arrived at the city.\n6\tFind the herald north of the city gate, in the First Circle (1978 Soldiers Pledged to Aragorn)\tThere is a herald north of the city gate of Minas Tirith, in the First Circle. Aragorn sent you to read his call for more soldiers to heralds who can reach the ears of the men that have now arrived at the city.\n7\tRead aloud Aragorn's call for soldiers (2003 Soldiers Pledged to Aragorn)\030Find the herald north of the city gate, in the First Circle (1978 Soldiers Pledged to Aragorn)\tThere is a herald north of the city gate of Minas Tirith, in the First Circle. Aragorn sent you to read his call for more soldiers to heralds who can reach the ears of the men that have now arrived at the city.\n8\tFind the herald north-west of the city gate, in the First Circle (2007 Soldiers Pledged to Aragorn)\tThere is a herald north-west of the city gate of Minas Tirith, in the First Circle. Aragorn sent you to read his call for more soldiers to heralds who can reach the ears of the men that have now arrived at the city.\n9\tRead aloud Aragorn's call for soldiers (2021 Soldiers Pledged to Aragorn)\030Find the herald north-west of the city gate, in the First Circle (2012 Soldiers Pledged to Aragorn)\tThere is a herald north-west of the city gate of Minas Tirith, in the First Circle. Aragorn sent you to read his call for more soldiers to heralds who can reach the ears of the men that have now arrived at the city.\n10\tTalk to Aragorn at his pavilion on the Pelennor Fields (2021 Soldiers Pledged to Aragorn)\tAragorn is at his pavilion east of Minas Tirith, after the Battle of Pelennor Fields.\n11\tTalk to Prince Imrahil at Aragorn's Pavilion\030Talk to Éomer at Aragorn's Pavilion\030Talk to Elfhelm at Aragorn's Pavilion\tImrahil, Éomer, and Elfhelm have returned to Aragorn's Pavilion with a count of the soldiers they have attained for Aragorn's march to Mordor.\n12\tTalk to Mithrandir at Aragorn's Pavilion\tMithrandir is at Aragorn's Pavilion east of Minas Tirith, after the Battle of Pelennor Fields.\n",
[2220]="7002FA13\n1\tTalk to Corudan\tCorudan is on Telain Neduil in the eastern side of Caras Galadhon. Galadriel has sent you to recruit Corudan as a guide along the Anduin as you investigate what has happened to the Fellowship.\n2\tTalk to Bordhrist and receive supplies of food for the journey\030Talk to Faengalph and arrange for a boat and paddles for the journey\tBordhrist is on Telain Galadhrim, and Faengalph is near the surrounding hedge not far from the entrance to Caras Galadhon, beneath Telain Glorelloth.\n3\tReturn to Corudan on Telain Neduil\tCorudan is waiting on Telain Neduil for you to return from arranging for a boat and supplies for the journey down the Anduin.\n4\tTalk to Nona near the House of Celeborn when you are ready to depart on your southward journey\tNona is on the flets near the House of Celeborn. Corudan has sent you to tell Nona you are ready to leave.\n",
[2221]="7002FA14\n1\tTalk to Corudan\tCorudan is on Telain Neduil in the eastern side of Caras Galadhon. Galadriel has sent you to recruit Corudan as a guide along the Anduin as you investigate what has happened to the Fellowship.\n2\tTalk to Bordhrist and receive supplies of food for the journey\030Talk to Faengalph and arrange for a boat and paddles for the journey\tBordhrist is on Telain Galadhrim, and Faengalph is near the surrounding hedge not far from the entrance to Caras Galadhon, beneath Telain Glorelloth.\n3\tReturn to Corudan on Telain Neduil\tCorudan is waiting on Telain Neduil for you to return from arranging for a boat and supplies for the journey down the Anduin.\n4\tTalk to Nona near the House of Celeborn when you are ready to depart on your southward journey\tNona is on the flets near the House of Celeborn. Corudan has sent you to tell Nona you are ready to leave.\n",
[2222]="700466A2\n1\tTalk to Celebrom on the Pelennor Fields, after the battle\030Talk to Limlaer on the Pelennor Fields, after the battle\030Talk to Ruhír on the Pelennor Fields, after the battle\030Talk to Culang on the Pelennor Fields, after the battle\tTrumpeters can be found on the Pelennor Fields, after the battle. Mithrandir has asked you to find trumpeters throughout the Pelennor Fields that might be willing to announce the departure of Aragorn's army from Minas Tirith with great noise and tumult.\n2\tGo to the western entrance of Osgiliath\tMithrandir asked you to travel to the western gate of Osgiliath after you gathered four trumpeters.\n3\tTalk to Nethadan at the west entrance of Osgiliath\tNethadan is at the western entrance to Osgiliath. You gathered a number of trumpeters to travel with Aragorn's army and announce the coming of King Elessar, and now should speak with some familiar faces at the entrance to Osgiliath.\n4\tTalk to Bandron at the west entrance of Osgiliath\tBandron is at the western entrance to Osgiliath. You gathered a number of trumpeters to travel with Aragorn's army and announce the coming of King Elessar, and now should speak with some familiar faces at the entrance to Osgiliath.\n5\tDefeat enemies remaining in Osgiliath (total: 8)\tSome enemies are still hiding in Osgiliath, waiting to jump out and attack the craftsmen responsible for repairing the city and the bridges. Bandron asked you to defeat some of the enemies lurking in Osgiliath in order to protect his interests.\n6\tGo to the eastern entrance of Osgiliath\tAragorn's army is passing through Osgiliath, and Mithrandir intended to meet you at the eastern gate of the city.\n7\tTalk to Mithrandir at the eastern entrance of Osgiliath\tMithrandir is astride Shadowfax at the east gate of Osgiliath.\n",
[2223]="7002FA19\n1\tTalk to Corudan\tCorudan is in Thinglad, in the Great River. You have come to Thinglad with Nona and Corudan, and should speak to Corudan, who wanted to recover the bow he lent to Fimloth.\n2\tDefeat Orcs in Thinglad while Nona and Corudan hunt for the bow as well (total: 6)\tOrcs can be found throughout Thinglad, alongside the Great River. Defeat them while Corudan and Nona do the same, and perhaps you will find Corudan's lost bow.\n3\tTalk to Corudan in Haldirith\tCorudan is at Haldirith, in Thinglad. You have searched for the Orc that took Corudan's bow, but did not find it.\n4\tTalk to Nona in Haldirith\tNona is in Haldirith, in Thinglad. You should speak to Nona about her experience hunting with Corudan.\n",
[2224]="700000A5\n1\tBring the scroll to Dwalin\tDwalin is at Thorin's Hall in Ered Luin. Elrond transcribed the scroll into Westron, but told you to seek the aid of Dwalin and the dwarves of Ered Luin in forging the pass-key to Carn Dûm.\n",
[2225]="7002FA18\n1\tTalk to Afic at the gate of Stangard to learn of Horn's whereabouts\tYou should speak with Afic, the guard at the gate of Stangard, about meeting with Horn.\n2\tTalk to Horn in Stangard\tHorn is atop the hill of Stangard. You have spoken with Afic, the guard at the gate of Stangard, and he had some inexplicably harsh words concerning Horn.\n3\tCollect Horn's harp from the Stangard tavern\030Collect Horn's writing supplies from Wada's house\tHorn is no longer welcome in Stangard, and has asked you to collect his harp from the Stangard Tavern, and his writing supplies from Wada's house.\n4\tBring his harp and writing supplies to Horn in Stangard\tHorn is in Stangard, waiting for you to bring him the items for which he asked.\n5\tTalk to Nona at Haldirith\tNona is in Haldirith, in Thinglad. Horn has decided to travel with you, and now you should go back to Nona so she can be told.\n6\tTalk to Corudan at Haldirith\tCorudan is at Haldirith, in Thinglad.\n",
[2226]="700466A3\n1\tTalk to Peregrin Took east of Osgiliath\tPeregrin Took is east of Osgiliath, before the road rises into the hills of Ithilien. Gandalf told you that Pippin is riding with the Host of the West, and might want to speak to you.\n2\tGo to the cross-roads in North Ithilien\tThe Cross-roads of the King are east of Osgiliath, in Ithilien. Aragorn and the Host of the West are marching into Ithilien, and plan to stop at the Cross-roads.\n3\tTalk to Aragorn at the cross-roads\tAragorn is at the Cross-roads of the King, in Ithilien.\n4\tDefeat foes throughout North Ithilien (total: 8)\030Tell Celebrom to announce the coming of the king\030Tell Limlaer to announce the coming of the king\030Tell Ruhír to announce the coming of the king\030Tell Culang to announce the coming of the king\tTrumpeters can be found at each of the roads that leave the Cross-roads of the King. After they have been told to sound their instruments, Aragorn asked you to defeat foes in North Ithilien and make your way to the Ranger hideout at Henneth Annûn.\n5\tFind the Ranger encampment at Henneth Annûn, in North Ithilien\tHenneth Annûn is located north of the Cross-roads, in North Ithilien. Aragorn asked you to travel ahead of the host and come to the Ranger hideout at Henneth Annûn.\n6\tTalk to Golasdín at Henneth Annûn\tHenneth Annûn is located far north of the Cross-roads, in North Ithilien. Aragorn asked you to move ahead of the host and come to the Ranger camp at Henneth Annûn.\n",
[2227]="700000A6\n1\tTalk to Keeper Brombard Foxtail\030Talk to Jon Brackenbrook\tKeeper Brombard Foxtail is at the Mathom-house in Michel Delving in the western part of the Shire. Jon Brackenbrook is in the town of Archet, north-east of Bree-town. Dwalin informed you that he needs a mithril nugget, which might be in the keeping of the Mathom-house in the Shire, and a key to cast a mould from, which might be obtained from Jon Brackenbrook, the new Captain of Archet.\n2\tBring the collected materials to Dwalin\tDwalin can be found in Thorin's Hall in Ered Luin. Dwalin sent you to get a mithril nugget from the Mathom-house in the Shire and a key to help in casting a mould from Jon Brackenbrook in Archet.\n3\tBring the collected materials to Litli\tLitli can be found by the forge near the throne of Thorin's Hall. Now that you have recovered the mithril and Éogan's key, Litli, one of Dwalin's smiths, can begin work on the key.\n4\tTalk to Dwalin\tDwalin can be found in Thorin's Hall in Ered Luin. Litli took the mithril from you and began heating it. However, he mentioned that shaping the mithril will be a problem, one that perhaps Dwalin can solve.\n",
[2228]="7002FA1A\n1\tTalk to Corudan at Haldirith and continue your journey down the Anduin\tCorudan is at Haldirith, in Thinglad, waiting to continue your journey down the Anduin.\n2\tTalk to Horn near the shadow of the Argonath\tYou have travelled with Corudan, Nona, and Horn to the Argonath, the Pillars of the Kings. Horn would like to speak with you.\n",
[2229]="700466A5\n1\tExplore the descending tunnel to Henneth Annûn\030Explore the main cavern of Henneth Annûn\030Explore the look-out point at the highest point of Henneth Annûn\030Do not enter the Forbidden Pool\tGolasdín welcomed you to explore the hidden path, the cave hideout, and the look-out at Henneth Annûn. He warned you not to enter the Forbidden Pool.\n2\tTalk to Aragorn outside Henneth Annûn\tAragorn is outside Henneth Annûn, and wishes to speak to you.\n3\tLook into the distance\030Find the look-out spot north-east of Henneth Annûn that Aragorn mentioned\tThe Rangers of Ithilien have a useful scouting location to the north-east of Henneth Annûn. Aragorn asked you to find Orndil and to scout ahead of the host for dangers posed by lurking enemies.\n4\tTalk to Orndil at the look-out spot\tOrndil is north-east of Henneth Annûn, and wishes to speak with you.\n5\tLook into the distance\030Find the look-out spot further to the north-east that Orndil mentioned\tOrndil thought he saw something to the north-east. You should investigate further.\n6\tTalk to Aragorn at Henneth Annûn\tAragorn is outside Henneth Annûn, and wishes to speak to you. You have learned that Orcs and Easterlings aim to ambush the Host of the West as it travels through Cirith Negen, and should report their plan to Aragorn.\n",
[2230]="700000A7\n1\tBring Thrór's Hammer to Dwalin\030Claim Thrór's Hammer from Skorgrím's tomb\tThrór's Hammer lies within the tomb of Skorgrím Dourhand. The tomb lies south-east of Thorin's Hall. Dwalin told you he needed a hammer that Thrór, Thorin's grandfather and last King Under the Mountain before the coming of Smaug, took with him into exile and which Thráin his son brought to the Blue Mountains.\n2\tBring Thrór's Hammer to Litli\tLitli can be found by the forges near the throne of Thorin's Hall in Ered Luin. You should take the hammer you found to Litli so that he can forge the key you need.\n",
[2231]="7002FA37\n1\tTalk to Nona in the shadow of the Argonath\tHorn has asked you to speak with Nona and Corudan before gathering sticks to make a campfire.\n2\tTalk to Corudan in the shadow of the Argonath\tHorn has asked you to speak with Nona and Corudan before gathering sticks to make a camp-fire.\n3\tCollect fallen sticks by the trees near the Argonath (total: 6)\tFallen sticks can be found near the trees not far from the Argonath. Horn has asked you to collect fallen sticks near the Argonath for preparing a camp-site.\n4\tBring the fallen sticks to Horn in the shadow of the Argonath\tHorn is by the beach near the Argonath. You have collected fallen sticks for making a camp-fire, as Horn requested.\n5\tRemove the remaining supplies from your boat near the Argonath\tYour boat is beached not far from the Argonath. Horn has asked you to remove the supplies from the boat.\n",
[2232]="700466A6\n1\tTalk to Hethradir by the look-out point over the Forbidden Pool\tHethradir is at the look-out point above the Forbidden Pool, near Henneth Annûn. Aragorn asked you to speak with Hethradir so he might select Rangers of Ithilien suitable for the task of ambushing the force that seeks to waylay the Host of the West at Cirith Negen.\n2\tTalk to Dagoras in the hidden cave at Henneth Annûn\tDagoras is in the hidden cave at Henneth Annûn. Aragorn asked you to speak with Dagoras so he might select Rangers of the Grey Company suitable for the task of ambushing the force that seeks to waylay the Host of the West at Cirith Negen.\n3\tTalk to Legolas in the hidden cave at Henneth Annûn\tLegolas is in the hidden cave at Henneth Annûn.\n4\tTalk to Legolas and travel to Cirith Negen\tLegolas is in the hidden cave at Henneth Annûn, ready to leave for Cirith Negen.\n5\tTalk to Dagoras in the hidden cave at Henneth Annûn\tDagoras is in the hidden cave at Henneth Annûn. You have helped to rout the intended ambush at Cirith Negen, and should now speak with Dagoras.\n6\tTalk to Aragorn outside Henneth Annûn\tAragorn is outside Henneth Annûn. Dagoras wanted you to raise his concerns with Aragorn concerning his experience in Cirith Negen.\n",
[2233]="700000A8\n1\tReturn the Carn Dûm gate key to Lorniel\tLorniel awaits your return at Gath Forthnír in eastern Angmar. You should return with the key to Lorniel.\n",
[2234]="7002FA38\n1\tTalk to Corudan in the shadow of the Argonath\tCorudan is in the shadow of the Argonath. You have divided up the supplies you brought from Lothlórien and should now speak with Corudan.\n2\tFind the lawn of Parth Galen, in the East Wall\tThe lawn of Parth Galen is south of the Argonath, on the south-western side of the lake of Nen Hithoel. Corudan believes you should begin your search for the Fellowship on the lawn of Parth Galen.\n3\tExamine the discarded pack and experience 'Session: The Breaking of the Fellowship' or read the shortened account at the Parth Galen camp-site instead\tA discarded pack lies partially buried in the grass of Parth Galen.\n4\tSomewhere within the East Wall, there are more signs of what happened to the Fellowship.\t\n5\tScour the beach near Parth Galen for clues and experience 'Two Hobbits'\tA great battle was fought at Dead Orc Glade... but not everyone came this way. Are there clues on the beach back near Parth Galen?\n6\tScour the beach near Parth Galen for clues and experience 'Session: Two Hobbits' or read the shortened account instead....\tSandy footprints on the beach near Parth Galen may give some clue as to what happened to the Fellowship!\n7\tTalk to Corudan in the shadow of the Argonath\tCorudan is in the shadow of the Argonath, in the East Wall. You have learned much about what befell the Fellowship, and should now return to tell the story to Corudan.\n",
[2235]="700466B3\n1\tTravel to Bâr Tarnaher, north-west of Henneth Annûn\tBâr Tarnaher is north-west of Henneth Annûn. The Rangers of Bâr Tarnaher have launched many attacks upon the Orcs from that ruin, and may know of any dangers to the Host of the West on the road ahead.\n2\tTalk to Legolas at Bâr Tarnaher\tLegolas is at the ruin of Bâr Tarnaher, in North Ithilien. You have come to the ruin of Bâr Tarnaher, but Legolas has found something amiss.\n3\tTalk to Bregaras at Bâr Tarnaher\tBregaras is at Bâr Tarnaher, north-west of Henneth Annûn in North Ithilien.\n4\tRetrieve Ranger supply caches east and north of Bâr Tarnaher (total: 5)\tRangers of Ithilien hid supply caches east and north of Bâr Tarnaher. Bregaras asked you to retrieve Ranger supply caches and bring them back to Bâr Tarnaher.\n5\tDeposit the collected supplies near Bregaras at Bâr Tarnaher\tBregaras asked you to leave the supplies you collected at Bâr Tarnaher.\n6\tTalk to Gimli at Bâr Tarnaher\tGimli is at Bâr Tarnaher, in North Ithilien.\n7\tTalk to Maegur at Bâr Tarnaher\030Talk to Unréth at Bâr Tarnaher\tUnréth and Maegur are at Bâr Tarnaher. Gimli noticed that the soldiers that came with you to Bâr Tarnaher have become increasingly troubled.\n8\tTalk to Aragorn at Henneth Annûn\tAragorn is at Henneth Annûn, in North Ithilien.\n9\tReassure worried soldiers at Henneth Annûn (total: 6)\tSoldiers of Aragorn's host can be found at Henneth Annûn. Aragorn asked you to try and bolster the courage of his men.\n10\tTalk to Aragorn at Henneth Annûn\tAragorn is at Henneth Annûn, in North Ithilien.\n11\tTalk to Aragorn at his camp on the border of Dagorlad\tAragorn is at his camp on the border between Dagorlad and North Ithilien.\n",
[2236]="7000019C\n1\tTalk to Lorniel\tLorniel awaits you at Gath Forthnír in eastern Angmar. Lorniel told you to speak with her again when you were ready to begin your raid on Carn Dûm. This quest is meant for a fellowship. If you choose to undertake this quest solo you will receive an inspiration bonus, but the challenge will be great.\n2\tTalk to Golodir\tGolodir is at Gath Forthnír. You have rescued Golodir, but at a terrible cost. The False King, Mordirith, appeared and slew her. You were able to weaken Mordirith and escape with Golodir back to Gath Forthnír.\n",
[2237]="700466B8\n1\tTalk to Mincham at Aragorn's camp on the Dagorlad border\030Talk to Faeron at Aragorn's camp on the Dagorlad border\tFaeron and Mincham can be found at Aragorn's camp on the border of Dagorlad. Aragorn has asked you to bring several of his Rangers on a mission to scout ahead of the host.\n2\tTalk to Langlas at Aragorn's camp on the Dagorlad border\tLanglas is at Aragorn's camp on the Dagorlad border. Langlas has called out to you. He has something to say before you leave to scout the plains of Dagorlad.\n3\tTalk to Aragorn at his camp on the Dagorlad border\tAragorn is at his camp on the border of Dagorlad.\n4\tTalk to Aragorn and scout the slag-hills of Dagorlad\tAragorn is at his camp on the border of Dagorlad.\n5\tTalk to Aragorn at his camp on the Dagorlad border\tAragorn is at his camp on the Dagorlad border.\n",
[2238]="7002FA3E\n1\tTalk to Ingild at Mansig's encampment, in the East Wall\tMansig's encampment is located south-west of the Argonath, on the border of the East Wall and the Norcrofts. A man named Ingild claims to have information of interest to you and your companions.\n2\tLook out over the plains of Rohan\030Travel to the ridge west of Mansig's encampment that forms the border of the East Wall with the Norcrofts\tTo the west of Mansig's encampment, a ridge overlooks the Norcrofts of Rohan. Ingild thinks you should look out over the plains and see if you can see the Uruks that fled East Wall.\n3\tTalk to Corudan\030Talk to Nona\030Talk to Horn\tYour companions stand on the ridge that overlooks the Norcrofts of Rohan, and want to speak with you concerning your next move.\n4\tTalk to Mansig at his encampment\tMansig's encampment is east of the ridge that forms the border between the East Wall and the Norcrofts. You should speak with Mansig about acquiring war-steeds that will allow you to follow the Uruks into Rohan.\n",
[2239]="70030314\n1\tTalk to Elfmar and help to train his men in the defence of Faldham\tElfmar is at the Mead Hall in Faldham. Elfmar would like you to train his men in combat, and also wishes to speak with you about your travels.\n2\tTalk to Elfmar in the Mead Hall of Faldham\tElfmar is in the Mead Hall of Faldham. You have helped to train many of Elfmar's men, and should now speak with him again.\n",
[2240]="70030313\n1\tTalk to Horn in Faldham\030Talk to Corudan in Faldham\030Talk to Nona in Faldham\tNona, Horn, and Corudan are outside the Mead Hall in Faldham. Elfmar has asked you to thank your companions from him before you leave for Eaworth.\n2\tDefeat mounted foes in the Entwash Vale (total: 6)\tEaworth is located in the Entwash Vale, halfway up the Entwash river. Elfmar has asked you to defeat mounted foes in the Entwash Vale as you travel to Eaworth.\n3\tTalk to Horn in Eaworth\tHorn is at the entrance to Eaworth, in the Entwash Vale.\n",
})
